lavender: Redmi Note 7 (SDM660) screen console and display on top of the base series

- early screen console: the ABL splash at 0x9d400000, 1080x2340 (same 32 MB block 0x9c000000
  the base series maps, so only the pointer and its alias move by 0x1400000)
- no access to SM6225 display registers (MDP, DSI, INTF): frames are CPU-copied into the splash
- sweetcpufreq defaults to off: that block is SM6225 only; the shim sets the Gold clock

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
index 94c7552..5738233 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ int sweet_cpufreq_max(void);
 int
 sweet_cpufreq_max(void)
 {
-	int on = 1;
+	int on = 0;     /* lavender: that is the SM6225 cpufreq block; the shim sets the Gold clock */
 	PE_parse_boot_argn("sweetcpufreq", &on, sizeof(on));
 	if (!on) {
 		return 0;
